For metrics question, think about -

Structured Approach (Categories):

Adoption/Reach: How many users are using it? (e.g., Feature activation rate, # active users of feature).

Engagement/Usage: How are they using it? How frequently? How deeply? (e.g., Time spent on relevant dashboard, # of interactions, # of custom rule configurations).

Effectiveness/Quality: Is the feature working as intended? Is it providing accurate and valuable output? (e.g., Anomaly detection precision/recall, Time to detection, False positive/negative rates).

Impact/Outcome: What are the business and user outcomes? This is often the most important category for Chorus View. (e.g., Reduction in spoilage/damage claims, On-time delivery improvement, Reduction in manual investigation time, Customer retention, NPS for feature).

Health/Performance: Is the feature stable and performant? (e.g., API latency, Uptime, Error rate).
